codex
Implemented the verified Track B generator, but it is not yet shippable because OpenRouter rejected every oracle call with HTTP 403 “Key limit exceeded.”

Files:

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1210.1451/gen_1210_1451.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1210.1451/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1210.1451/README.md)
- [Bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1210.1451/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1210.1451/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1210.1451/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

The family uses Section 2.2, Theorem 1 of the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1210.1451): square homogeneous resultant systems encoding signed Partition. Prouhet–Thue–Morse identities construct exact rational roots before randomization.

Local results:

- G1–G9(c): pass
- Exact hard density: `1970 / 2^32 ≈ 4.587e-7`
- Five attacks: `0/8` successes each
- Reference bitset DP: `8/8`, 21,876,480 estimated word updates
- Answer cap: 312 characters, 78 tokens, 66 atoms
- G8: 140/140 symmetry checks

No `REJECTED.md` was created because this is an external credential failure, not a G/H/V failure. After restoring the OpenRouter allowance, rerun the bare and two G9 arms before submission.
